<http://data.silknow.org/object/f8bc08b8-34ed-3015-a731-5a6d3860c217/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nINSIGNIA OF THE ORDER OF THE GARTER<br>\nThe Order of the Garter, founded on St George's day in about 1348, is still Britain's highest order of chivalry. Charles I promoted this ancient order and introduced an embroidered star to be worn in public by Knights of the Garter on their cloaks. This star is embroidered with silver thread, but gold and even diamonds were also used. The badge was first introduced by Henry VIII and was worn on a blue riband or sash. It is known as the Lesser George and replaced the official Great George for everyday use. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f8bc08b8-34ed-3015-a731-5a6d3860c217> .

